".claude/docs/services/escher-driver.md": [
63,
"- The command line, through the real `escher-session` binary (seven_guis, unix only): `host_binary` (the host role on `counter`; a host that cannot serve; nine argv rows that are no command), `host_log` (a host on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace` while three calls run: one span line per call, no id, name or typed text, under both builds), `host_timer` (the timer host moved by a hosted `advance`), `cli_commands` (every driver command as a process on the four tasks: fields, refusals by status `1`, usage by `2`, session errors by `3`) and `cli_flow` (two POSIX `sh` flows, `counter.sh` and `flight.sh`); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `mcp_server` (the `mcp` role completes the Counter flow by tool calls alone; protocol errors run nothing and leak nothing; unix only, a snapshot equal through MCP and the command line) and `mcp_log` (the role at `RUST_LOG=trace`: no id, name or typed text, one `tool_call` line per call, under both builds), not unix-gated but the comparison — and in process `stand_mcp_tools` (blitz-tests; the flow through `serve_mcp` in both layout modes, one `tool_call` span the parent of each `command`; since 2026-10-12-self-description every cause a tool call reaches served with its remedy, `covered` on an overlay fixture, and `help` answered by the server, parenting no `command` span) and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, `stand_mcp_masked` (a password typed through an MCP `type` reads `MASKED_VALUE` and never the typed text, role `PasswordInput` with a non-empty name, in both layout modes; it declares no `mod session_common;`). Mutation controls in `escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/evidence/controls.md` (five)."
],
".claude/docs/services/escher-telemetry.md": [
46,
"- `.claude/rules/observability.md` · `.claude/docs/obs-summary.md` · `.claude/rules/security.md` (env reads)"
]
},
